# Phase 6 behaviour check for inc-30ps: Minor Drain becomes a touch spell.
# Read by tools/check_minor_drain_touch.sh.
#
# WHAT "CANNOT BE CAST AT RANGE" MEANS HERE, AND WHY IT IS NOT DRIVEN LIVE.
# Player::KY_CMD_MAGIC (src/Player.cpp) calls
#   MyTerm->EffectPrompt(e, TEFF(e.eID)->ef.qval | ((MMFeats(sp) & MM_PROJECT) ? Q_DIR : 0))
# and TextTerm::EffectPrompt (src/Term.cpp) opens with
#   if (fl == 0 && ...) fl = TEFF(e.eID)->ef.qval;
#   typ = fl & 0x000F; ... if (!typ) return true;
# Minor Drain's qval is now empty and it is not a projected ability, so this
# call is made with fl == 0 and returns true immediately: no prompt, no
# target, no way to name a square or a distant creature. That is a direct
# reading of the dispatch code, not something a key script can demonstrate
# more convincingly than the absence of qval already does -- so
# tools/check_line_of_fire_effects.sh's Minor Drain assertions (aval:
# AR_TOUCH, no qval field) are the proof of "cannot be cast at range", and
# this script proves the other half: the touch still delivers.
#
# WHY WIZARD MODE. No scripted walk can be relied on to find both a known
# spell and an adjacent monster, so wizard mode supplies both, following the
# pattern already proven in tools/keys/sanctuary-strike.keys:
#   * "Learn Any Spell" (src/Debug.cpp:850) takes a typed name and sets
#     SP_KNOWN|SP_PRIMAL|SP_INNATE. An innate spell costs no mana, so this
#     needs no spellbook and no mana pool math -- irrelevant to what is being
#     measured. It still dispatches through Player::CastSpell exactly like a
#     normally-learned spell (EV_INVOKE instead of EV_CAST; both reach the
#     same Magic::ATouch/MagicStrike machinery Player::CastSpell uses).
#   * "Wizard Mode Switches" row 11, Freeze Monsters, stops the goblin doing
#     anything of its own, so only the player's own touch attack moves HP.
#   * "Monster Summoning" places a goblin at a KNOWN distance: TWO squares
#     east (RIGHT RIGHT ENTER), deliberately out of melee reach, so casting
#     while not adjacent has nothing it could touch.
#
# THE ORACLE is the game's own combat text. A touch-attack swing prints text
# no ordinary unarmed punch does -- "you try to touch a <target>" -- because
# it is resolved on the A_TUCH branch of Creature::RAttack (src/Fight.cpp),
# which only exists while TOUCH_ATTACK is armed. That branch is reached only
# once the caster is adjacent, so:
#
#   before-cast   goblin two squares east -- out of reach, nothing to touch
#   after-cast    immediately after casting -- no prompt, no message, no
#                 target: the touch is armed and nothing has been delivered
#   touch-1..N    close the gap by one square, then bump-attack the goblin
#                 once per dump, until the message names a touch outcome
#                 other than a miss ("...but miss" is a real touch ATTEMPT
#                 that did not land, and is retried; anything else -- landing
#                 and dealing 1-4 points, or landing and killing an 8 HP
#                 goblin outright -- is the spell actually firing)
#
# A landed touch proves the heal fired too, without needing to read it off
# the status line (the caster starts and stays at full HP, so a 1-4 point
# heal is invisible there): Minor Drain's only handler is
#   On Event EV_MAGIC_HIT { EActor->cHP = min(...,EActor->cHP + e.vDmg); }
# and Creature::RAttack's own touch-discharge code (src/Fight.cpp, the
# "AfterEffects" block) calls this exact event, unconditionally, the moment
# a touch attack lands -- there is no code path where the goblin takes the
# spell's damage without this same line also running.
#
# A run against the PRE-FIX tree (aval: AR_BOLT, qval: Q_DIR|Q_TAR|Q_LOC)
# does not reach after-cast cleanly: casting opens the "Select direction,
# location or target:" prompt this script never answers, so @dump:after-cast
# photographs that prompt instead of a normal map screen, and the run ends
# with the prompt still open and none of the later dumps taken. That is the
# RED failure tools/check_minor_drain_touch.sh reads.

@include chargen-mage.keys
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Minor Drain"
ENTER
@dump:before-learn

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT RIGHT ENTER
@dump:before-cast

m
@choose "Minor Drain"
@dump:after-cast

RIGHT
@dump:closed-distance
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-1
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-2
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-3
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-4
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-5
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:touch-6
